    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#turkmen">Turkmen</a> tribal dynasty that reunited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#iran">Iran</a> in the 1790s and ruled from Tehran, which it made the capital.</li><li>Wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#russia">Russia</a> cost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#iran">Iran</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#caucasus">Caucasus</a> by 1828, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#britain">Britain</a> and Russia competed for influence over the weak state.</li><li>The Constitutional Revolution of 1906 created a parliament; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#reza-shah">Reza Khan</a>’s coup of 1921 led to the dynasty’s fall in 1925.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Naser al-Din Shah was an enthusiastic photographer who took and developed pictures himself, and thousands of Qajar-era photographs survive in the Golestan Palace collections.</p></aside>
    </section>

